WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:03.734
-The grand jury
investigating Donald Trump's

00:00:03.734 --> 00:00:05.367
hush money payment
to Stormy Daniels

00:00:05.367 --> 00:00:07.501
heard from yet another
key witness yesterday,

00:00:07.501 --> 00:00:09.100
in a sign that
the Manhattan district attorney

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.000
is bolstering his case
against Trump

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.868
ahead of
an expected indictment.

00:00:12.868 --> 00:00:15.501
Trump, meanwhile, appeared on
Fox News to sweat and grimace

00:00:15.501 --> 00:00:16.901
and be weird as usual,

00:00:16.901 --> 00:00:19.534
and also to attack
his likely rival

00:00:19.534 --> 00:00:21.200
for the GOP nomination,
Ron DeSantis.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.701
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:23.701 --> 00:00:26.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:26.701 --> 00:00:28.100
I feel like a lot of us

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:30.267
are waiting
for some cinematic moment

00:00:30.267 --> 00:00:31.601
when Donald Trump
gets arrested

00:00:31.601 --> 00:00:32.968
while forgetting
that in real life,

00:00:32.968 --> 00:00:35.400
nothing is that satisfying.
If Donald Trump was Jason,

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.734
not only would he not die
at the end of the movie,

00:00:37.734 --> 00:00:39.467
he would be allowed
to hold public rallies

00:00:39.467 --> 00:00:41.400
where he complains that campers
don't skinny dip

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.267
like they used to.

00:00:43.267 --> 00:00:44.767
It just seems like
Trump's been doing

00:00:44.767 --> 00:00:46.567
so many crimes for so long.

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:49.100
I bet if you zoomed in
on that infamous photo of him

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:50.267
coming down the escalator

00:00:50.267 --> 00:00:52.234
the day he announced
his first candidacy,

00:00:52.234 --> 00:00:55.601
you'd see he had shoplifted a
pair of earrings from Claire's.

00:00:55.601 --> 00:00:57.033
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.033 --> 00:00:58.934
That's why when he was
at the podium,

00:00:58.934 --> 00:01:01.734
you could hear
a store alarm going off.

00:01:01.734 --> 00:01:03.834
[ Alarm blaring ]

00:01:05.367 --> 00:01:07.868
So, it's another day, and we're
all still waiting to find out

00:01:07.868 --> 00:01:09.367
if and when Trump
will be arrested.

00:01:09.367 --> 00:01:11.000
The news has basically
just become

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:14.033
the NORAD Santa tracker,
except for Trump's indictment.

00:01:14.033 --> 00:01:16.601
Just a little circle
in the middle,

00:01:16.601 --> 00:01:17.834
middle of the Atlantic Ocean.

00:01:17.834 --> 00:01:20.100
Meanwhile, the grand jury
weighing a possible

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:21.868
Trump indictment
is still doing its work.

00:01:21.868 --> 00:01:24.000
Yesterday, they heard
from yet another key player

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:26.601
in the hush money scandal,
in a sign that the Manhattan DA

00:01:26.601 --> 00:01:28.901
is bolstering his case
against Trump.

00:01:28.901 --> 00:01:30.901
-A key player
in the Trump hush money probe

00:01:30.901 --> 00:01:33.267
just met with
a Manhattan grand jury

00:01:33.267 --> 00:01:35.400
investigating
the former president.

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:36.801
A source confirms to CNN

00:01:36.801 --> 00:01:39.868
that former National Enquirer
publisher David Pecker

00:01:39.868 --> 00:01:42.601
appeared before the panel
earlier this afternoon.

00:01:42.601 --> 00:01:45.434
-Sources close to
the investigation tell CBS News

00:01:45.434 --> 00:01:48.000
that David Pecker's
appearance today is a sign

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.067
District Attorney Alvin Bragg
might be finalizing a case

00:01:51.067 --> 00:01:53.234
against former president
Donald Trump.

00:01:53.234 --> 00:01:55.868
In 2016, it was Pecker
who encouraged efforts

00:01:55.868 --> 00:01:58.701
by then candidate Trump
and Michael Cohen

00:01:58.701 --> 00:02:00.601
to prevent damaging stories
about Trump

00:02:00.601 --> 00:02:01.801
from being published.

00:02:01.801 --> 00:02:04.033
-Yesterday's convening
of this two-month-long

00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:06.234
grand jury probe
appeared to center around

00:02:06.234 --> 00:02:08.434
hearing testimony
from David Pecker.

00:02:08.434 --> 00:02:10.467
Pecker is a central figure
in this drama,

00:02:10.467 --> 00:02:12.667
as you pointed out,
about those hush money payments

00:02:12.667 --> 00:02:14.501
to adult film actress
Stormy Daniels.

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:16.000
In his role at the time

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:17.968
as publisher
of The National Enquirer

00:02:17.968 --> 00:02:20.367
and a friend of
then candidate Donald Trump,

00:02:20.367 --> 00:02:23.934
he helped broker
the original $130,000 payment.

00:02:23.934 --> 00:02:25.267
-That's right.
The grand jury heard

00:02:25.267 --> 00:02:26.934
from a key player
in Trump's corrupt scheme

00:02:26.934 --> 00:02:28.701
to broker a secretive
hush money payment

00:02:28.701 --> 00:02:29.901
to conceal an illicit affair

00:02:29.901 --> 00:02:31.734
just weeks before
a presidential election

00:02:31.734 --> 00:02:34.133
and then disguised
those payments by lying

00:02:34.133 --> 00:02:36.534
about what they were for.
It's a damning development

00:02:36.534 --> 00:02:38.033
in what is already
a serious case

00:02:38.033 --> 00:02:40.267
that could very well result
in a historic, first-ever

00:02:40.267 --> 00:02:41.868
indictment
of a former president.

00:02:41.868 --> 00:02:43.267
But my main takeaway
is this --

00:02:43.267 --> 00:02:45.100
I can't believe

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:46.767
this guy's last name is Pecker.

00:02:46.767 --> 00:02:48.300
It's...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:52.634
...a story about Trump
having sex with a porn star,

00:02:52.634 --> 00:02:56.000
and a key player's last name,
it's Pecker.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:58.133
So I guess in this way,
the Trump case,

00:02:58.133 --> 00:02:59.667
you know, it is cinematic,

00:02:59.667 --> 00:03:01.334
but it's like a bad '80s comedy,

00:03:01.334 --> 00:03:04.300
like "Bachelor Party"
or "Porky's."

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:07.601
"Hey, Pecker, you want to help
us out with little problem?"

00:03:07.601 --> 00:03:10.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.567 --> 00:03:12.467
Who else has the grand jury
heard from?

00:03:12.467 --> 00:03:13.601
Trump's bookkeeper,

00:03:13.601 --> 00:03:15.534
Mike Schlong?

00:03:15.534 --> 00:03:18.133
So, the grand jury heard
from another key witness,

00:03:18.133 --> 00:03:21.167
although I use that term
very loosely,

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:24.334
given that at this point,
we are all key witnesses.

00:03:24.334 --> 00:03:26.234
I mean, we've heard
from Michael Cohen,

00:03:26.234 --> 00:03:27.601
we've heard
from Stormy Daniels.

00:03:27.601 --> 00:03:30.033
We've even seen the actual
check that Trump wrote.

00:03:30.033 --> 00:03:31.934
Only Trump is stupid enough
to pay hush money

00:03:31.934 --> 00:03:34.501
to cover up an affair,
but sign his name to a check.

00:03:34.501 --> 00:03:37.501
Just fill up an envelope
with unmarked bills

00:03:37.501 --> 00:03:39.067
like a normal criminal,
you dingus.

00:03:39.067 --> 00:03:42.601
This is like if Gwyneth Paltrow
showed up to her trial

00:03:42.601 --> 00:03:45.100
wearing a shirt that said,
"I'm a really bad skier."

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:46.267
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.267 --> 00:03:48.434
And then on her way
to the witness stand,

00:03:48.434 --> 00:03:50.767
she just plows into the bailiff.

00:03:50.767 --> 00:03:52.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:54.100
By the way, it should be noted,

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:57.167
paying hush money
is not itself a crime.

00:03:57.167 --> 00:03:58.667
I mean, it's not, like, cool,

00:03:58.667 --> 00:04:00.567
especially if you do it
two weeks

00:04:00.567 --> 00:04:02.767
before a pivotal presidential
election that will determine

00:04:02.767 --> 00:04:04.934
who gets to fill three seats
on the Supreme Court.

00:04:04.934 --> 00:04:07.634
But it's not necessarily
against the law,

00:04:07.634 --> 00:04:09.100
if you do it the right way.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:11.367
The problem is Trump tried to
cover it up by lying about it.

00:04:11.367 --> 00:04:13.100
And you don't need
to take my word for it.

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:16.000
Here once again is star witness
Rudy Giuliani --

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:18.100
And just in general, a star.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:19.200
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:21.734
He's just got that "it" factor,
you know?

00:04:21.734 --> 00:04:23.267
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.267 --> 00:04:27.100
...explaining how the whole
scheme worked back in 2018.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:28.901
-That money was not
campaign money.

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:32.067
Sorry, I'm giving you a fact now
that you don't know.

00:04:32.067 --> 00:04:34.167
It's not campaign money.

00:04:34.167 --> 00:04:37.868
No campaign finance violation.

00:04:37.868 --> 00:04:40.367
'Cause they funneled it through
the law firm?

00:04:40.367 --> 00:04:43.033
-Funneled through a law firm
and the president repaid it.

00:04:43.033 --> 00:04:46.367
When I heard Cohen's
retainer of $35,000

00:04:46.367 --> 00:04:48.701
when he was doing no work
for the president,

00:04:48.701 --> 00:04:50.601
I said, well, that's
how he's repaying,

00:04:50.601 --> 00:04:53.834
that's how he's repaying it,
with a little profit

00:04:53.834 --> 00:04:57.167
and a little margin
for paying taxes, for Michael.

00:04:57.167 --> 00:04:59.501
-Yeah, that's the crime.

00:04:59.501 --> 00:05:01.234
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.234 --> 00:05:04.567
You can't funnel money from your
business to your personal fixer

00:05:04.567 --> 00:05:06.534
to cover up an affair
with an adult film star

00:05:06.534 --> 00:05:08.634
to help your presidential
campaign two weeks before

00:05:08.634 --> 00:05:11.567
an election and then lie
about what the money was for

00:05:11.567 --> 00:05:13.667
by saying it's just a retainer
for your attorney.

00:05:13.667 --> 00:05:16.767
It's the same reason you'd get
in trouble with your spouse

00:05:16.767 --> 00:05:19.033
if you put an event in your
Google Calendar called

00:05:19.033 --> 00:05:22.167
"Meeting with 'Pecker'
for work stuff,

00:05:22.167 --> 00:05:24.167
not a euphemism for sex."

00:05:24.167 --> 00:05:25.801
-Although -- although,

00:05:25.801 --> 00:05:28.501
there is another part
of that clip that I love,

00:05:28.501 --> 00:05:31.667
where Rudy explains
why he's so confident

00:05:31.667 --> 00:05:33.300
this is all aboveboard.

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:36.701
-Funneled through a law firm,
and the president repaid it.

00:05:36.701 --> 00:05:38.501
-Oh, I didn't know -- He did?
-Yep.

00:05:38.501 --> 00:05:40.334
-There's no campaign
finance law.

00:05:40.334 --> 00:05:41.834
-Zero.

00:05:41.834 --> 00:05:43.968
-So, the President --
-Just like every -- Sean --

00:05:43.968 --> 00:05:46.167
-So, this decision
was made by...?

00:05:46.167 --> 00:05:48.234
-Everybody -- Everybody was
nervous about this

00:05:48.234 --> 00:05:49.868
from the very beginning.
I wasn't.

00:05:49.868 --> 00:05:53.200
-If everyone around you
is nervous and you're not,

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:54.868
you're either a Navy SEAL

00:05:54.868 --> 00:05:56.267
or you're a moron.

00:05:56.267 --> 00:05:58.934
And that ain't no Navy SEAL.

00:05:58.934 --> 00:06:00.367
Although he does --

00:06:00.367 --> 00:06:02.400
you guys, he does dye his hair

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:04.767
with Thompson's WaterSeal,
so that...

00:06:04.767 --> 00:06:06.267
[ Laughter ]

00:06:06.267 --> 00:06:07.767
This whole thing
is a reminder --

00:06:07.767 --> 00:06:09.367
When Rudy tells you
not to worry,

00:06:09.367 --> 00:06:11.067
it's time to [bleep] panic.

00:06:11.067 --> 00:06:12.567
If Rudy's...
[ Laughter ]

00:06:12.567 --> 00:06:13.734
If Rudy is your lawyer

00:06:13.734 --> 00:06:15.100
and he tells you
he's not nervous,

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:17.100
the SWAT team is en route.

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:18.100
[ Laughter ]

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:19.601
I mean, look at this man.

00:06:19.601 --> 00:06:23.467
He looks like he just found out
he's on this show.

00:06:23.467 --> 00:06:25.133
[ Laughter ]

00:06:25.133 --> 00:06:26.601
[As Giuliani] Uh-oh!

00:06:26.601 --> 00:06:28.100
[ Laughs ]

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:29.701
I'm over Seth Meyers' shoulder?

00:06:29.701 --> 00:06:31.367
This can't be good.

00:06:31.367 --> 00:06:33.367
[ Laughter ]

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:37.801
[Normal voice] So, Rudy
basically confessed

00:06:37.801 --> 00:06:39.734
the entire crime
on national television,

00:06:39.734 --> 00:06:42.000
and there is an abundance
of hard evidence to back it up.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:43.834
But Trump supporters
and right-wing media

00:06:43.834 --> 00:06:45.300
want you to think

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:48.300
this was all just an innocent
little record-keeping mistake.

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:50.801
-They better not put
my president in prison.

00:06:50.801 --> 00:06:54.901
He represents
74 million Americans.

00:06:54.901 --> 00:06:56.534
And if he's the nominee,

00:06:56.534 --> 00:07:00.934
you're putting 74 million votes
in prison.

00:07:00.934 --> 00:07:02.834
And that's how I see it.
-Really?

00:07:02.834 --> 00:07:05.434
-On a bookkeeping charge.

00:07:05.434 --> 00:07:06.767
-First of all,

00:07:06.767 --> 00:07:08.767
I love one of the co-hosts
just saying, "Really?"

00:07:08.767 --> 00:07:11.901
Because that is
the appropriate reaction.

00:07:11.901 --> 00:07:13.234
It's insane to say

00:07:13.234 --> 00:07:17.701
you're putting
74 million votes in prison.

00:07:17.701 --> 00:07:20.367
Although it's very funny
to imagine a Trump supporter

00:07:20.367 --> 00:07:21.767
showing up
to a federal penitentiary

00:07:21.767 --> 00:07:23.300
and saying,
"I'm here to see my vote.

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:24.634
It's in prison."

00:07:24.634 --> 00:07:26.400
And he has to have
a teary-eyed conversation

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:29.734
through a glass partition
with a piece of paper.

00:07:29.734 --> 00:07:32.000
"Don't worry about it.
I'm gonna get you out of here."

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:33.100
[ Laughter ]

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:34.434
-With Trump under
at least four different

00:07:34.434 --> 00:07:35.701
criminal investigations

00:07:35.701 --> 00:07:37.367
and after he tanked
three successive elections,

00:07:37.367 --> 00:07:38.734
including last year's midterms,

00:07:38.734 --> 00:07:40.801
there's been a question as to
whether right-wing media

00:07:40.801 --> 00:07:42.968
would finally pivot
away from him

00:07:42.968 --> 00:07:44.734
and embrace Florida Governor
Ron DeSantis.

00:07:44.734 --> 00:07:46.601
It started to seem like
maybe that would happen

00:07:46.601 --> 00:07:49.067
when Fox started
airing glowing profiles

00:07:49.067 --> 00:07:51.000
of DeSantis
and fawning interviews with him,

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:53.601
including one interview
where Fox host Brian Kilmeade

00:07:53.601 --> 00:07:56.234
literally had a catch with
DeSantis on a baseball field.

00:07:56.234 --> 00:07:58.801
Now, I could say they look
like a couple of dorks,

00:07:58.801 --> 00:08:01.534
and I'd be right,
but in fairness, it's hard

00:08:01.534 --> 00:08:03.801
not to look like a dork playing
baseball past a certain age.

00:08:03.801 --> 00:08:06.133
I mean, Barack Obama
was our coolest president.

00:08:06.133 --> 00:08:07.601
He made a three-pointer
on camera.

00:08:07.601 --> 00:08:09.300
He wears sunglasses
and an open collar.

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:10.667
He hangs out
with Bruce Springsteen.

00:08:10.667 --> 00:08:12.167
And yet even he looked
like a dork

00:08:12.167 --> 00:08:13.334
when he was throwing
a baseball.

00:08:13.334 --> 00:08:14.634
[ Laughter ]

00:08:14.634 --> 00:08:16.501
I mean, if baseball
could do that to Barack Obama,

00:08:16.501 --> 00:08:18.000
Ron DeSantis,
he never had a chance.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:20.901
So, after that interview
with DeSantis,

00:08:20.901 --> 00:08:23.300
there was speculation
that Fox might turn on Trump.

00:08:23.300 --> 00:08:25.534
Some of Trump's goons
have also been exiled

00:08:25.534 --> 00:08:27.033
to smaller right-wing networks,

00:08:27.033 --> 00:08:28.968
like, you know,
the aforementioned Rudy,

00:08:28.968 --> 00:08:30.367
who, as we just told you,

00:08:30.367 --> 00:08:31.934
went on Fox a few years ago
and confessed to everything.

00:08:31.934 --> 00:08:34.334
It seems like Rudy's been
unofficially banned from Fox.

00:08:34.334 --> 00:08:36.767
So now when he wants to comment
on the hush money case,

00:08:36.767 --> 00:08:38.834
he has to go on lesser-known
right-wing outlets,

00:08:38.834 --> 00:08:41.200
where things just seem
to go horribly wrong.

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:42.567
Like this interview
from last week

00:08:42.567 --> 00:08:44.334
where the host
began praising him

00:08:44.334 --> 00:08:47.200
and then Rudy had some very
embarrassing technical problems.

00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:49.901
-Mayor Rudy Giuliani,
always amazing to see you.

00:08:49.901 --> 00:08:51.434
Love you.
Sorry.

00:08:51.434 --> 00:08:53.734
I'm -- I'm just
so honored always,

00:08:53.734 --> 00:08:56.200
as always,
to interview you, sir.

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:58.868
[ Laughter ]

00:08:58.868 --> 00:09:01.334
Mayor Giuliani, what would --
what would you have done

00:09:01.334 --> 00:09:02.934
if this case was
brought before you?

00:09:02.934 --> 00:09:04.434
You prosecuted a lot of cases.

00:09:04.434 --> 00:09:06.601
Before you became
New York City mayor,

00:09:06.601 --> 00:09:08.701
you were a, you know,
a prosecutor.

00:09:08.701 --> 00:09:10.067
What would you have done
if somebody said,

00:09:10.067 --> 00:09:13.200
"Here's the case,
prosecute this"?

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:15.234
-Well, here's
what I would have done.

00:09:15.234 --> 00:09:17.033
I would have told them
to go to hell.

00:09:17.033 --> 00:09:18.367
[ Audio cuts out ]

00:09:18.367 --> 00:09:20.033
I had it happen...
[ Audio cuts out ]

00:09:20.033 --> 00:09:21.834
[ Laughter ]

00:09:23.534 --> 00:09:26.234
-It looks like we're having
some audio issues there.

00:09:27.968 --> 00:09:33.567
-We go way back to 19...
19...

00:09:36.033 --> 00:09:38.534
-Oh, my God.

00:09:38.534 --> 00:09:41.133
Maybe Rudy's lawyer told him,
"Instead of talking,

00:09:41.133 --> 00:09:44.267
just pretend like
you're talking, and be quiet."

00:09:44.267 --> 00:09:45.601
[As Giuliani]
Oh, that sounds...

00:09:45.601 --> 00:09:47.267
[ Mouthing words ]

00:09:47.267 --> 00:09:48.767
[ Laughter ]

00:09:48.767 --> 00:09:50.801
Seriously, what happened there?

00:09:50.801 --> 00:09:53.267
Did they turn off the Wi-Fi
at Rudy's nursing home?

00:09:53.267 --> 00:09:55.968
This is like watching
one of those live webcams

00:09:55.968 --> 00:09:57.167
from the San Diego Zoo

00:09:57.167 --> 00:10:00.334
where the monkeys
start humping the camera.

00:10:00.334 --> 00:10:02.334
Although, I have to say,
I think the hand over the camera

00:10:02.334 --> 00:10:04.200
is actually an improvement
over seeing Rudy's face.

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:05.767
Just draw some eyes
and a mouth over it.

00:10:05.767 --> 00:10:08.334
There you go.
Problem solved.

00:10:08.334 --> 00:10:11.567
Also, I love that when
[bleep] starts going sideways,

00:10:11.567 --> 00:10:14.000
not only doesn't Rudy
stop the interview,

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:15.334
they don't stop it either.

00:10:15.334 --> 00:10:17.334
It's like they're
slowly realizing,

00:10:17.334 --> 00:10:21.334
"Yeah, we should have known
it would go this way."

00:10:21.334 --> 00:10:22.801
[ Laughter ]

00:10:22.801 --> 00:10:25.033
So that's basically where Trump
and his inner circle are at.

00:10:25.033 --> 00:10:27.801
And yet last night, Fox host
Sean Hannity chose to give Trump

00:10:27.801 --> 00:10:29.667
a platform to ramble about
his usual bull[bleep]

00:10:29.667 --> 00:10:32.567
without any pushback at all.
For example, last week,

00:10:32.567 --> 00:10:34.901
Trump tried to menace
investigators into backing down

00:10:34.901 --> 00:10:37.067
when he threatened death and
destruction if he's arrested.

00:10:37.067 --> 00:10:39.334
But last night,
he claimed ludicrously

00:10:39.334 --> 00:10:41.601
that he wasn't threatening
death and destruction --

00:10:41.601 --> 00:10:44.467
he was just saying
he was scared of it.

00:10:44.467 --> 00:10:46.501
-I will say this
with death and destruction --

00:10:46.501 --> 00:10:47.868
I didn't say
death and destruction.

00:10:47.868 --> 00:10:50.133
I said I'm afraid.
-The possibility. Yeah.

00:10:50.133 --> 00:10:52.300
-I said I'm afraid
that if they do this,

00:10:52.300 --> 00:10:53.934
which is a fake prosecution...

00:10:53.934 --> 00:10:56.100
I didn't say,
"Do something bad."

00:10:56.100 --> 00:10:59.200
I say I am afraid
that people will do something

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:01.200
because people are
very angry about it.

00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:02.634
-Yeah, he didn't say,
"I'm gonna burn down

00:11:02.634 --> 00:11:04.634
your restaurant."
He said, "It would be a shame

00:11:04.634 --> 00:11:08.133
if something were to happen
to your nice restaurant

00:11:08.133 --> 00:11:10.267
in the middle of the night,
say, 2 a.m. or so.

00:11:10.267 --> 00:11:11.701
Capisce?"

00:11:11.701 --> 00:11:13.200
[ Laughter ]

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:14.634
But my favorite part
of that interview

00:11:14.634 --> 00:11:16.801
came when Trump totally
went off on DeSantis

00:11:16.801 --> 00:11:19.267
and told an elaborate fantasy
about DeSantis begging him

00:11:19.267 --> 00:11:21.901
for his endorsement for governor
back in 2018.

00:11:21.901 --> 00:11:24.267
-So, what happened with Ron
is the following.

00:11:24.267 --> 00:11:25.601
He came to see me.

00:11:25.601 --> 00:11:27.734
He was getting killed.
He was being crushed.

00:11:27.734 --> 00:11:31.033
Ron came to see me,
tears in his eyes.

00:11:31.033 --> 00:11:33.501
He said, "I need you
to do me a big favor."

00:11:33.501 --> 00:11:37.334
First he asked for the meeting.
Then he asked me for the favor.

00:11:37.334 --> 00:11:39.400
I said, "What's the favor?"

00:11:39.400 --> 00:11:41.067
"Would you endorse me?"

00:11:41.067 --> 00:11:43.167
So I said,
"Let's give it a shot, Ron."

00:11:43.167 --> 00:11:46.033
Okay?
And he was desperate.

00:11:46.033 --> 00:11:48.868
I said, "Okay."
I gave him a nice endorsement.

00:11:48.868 --> 00:11:50.868
I said, "You write out what
you'd like and let me see it."

00:11:50.868 --> 00:11:52.467
He wrote it out.
I thought it was terrible.

00:11:52.467 --> 00:11:54.033
I changed it, made it great.

00:11:54.033 --> 00:11:56.534
I gave him a great endorsement.

00:11:56.534 --> 00:11:59.467
From the moment
I pressed that button,

00:11:59.467 --> 00:12:01.634
he blew the guy away.
The race was over.

00:12:01.634 --> 00:12:04.000
-Personally, I'm just so glad
"tears in his eyes" is back.

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:05.934
I hope he keeps
adding to the story.

00:12:05.934 --> 00:12:07.400
[As Trump] I was in
the Oval Office one day

00:12:07.400 --> 00:12:09.234
and a guy came up to me --
little guy, tiny guy,

00:12:09.234 --> 00:12:11.167
tears in his eyes, running...

00:12:11.167 --> 00:12:13.734
The tears were running down
his face and onto the floor,

00:12:13.734 --> 00:12:16.601
where they made puddles around
his fancy, little white boots.

00:12:16.601 --> 00:12:18.934
Little white boots.
Splish-splash.

00:12:18.934 --> 00:12:20.534
His little boots
were going splish-splash

00:12:20.534 --> 00:12:22.467
in the tears he had cried.

00:12:22.467 --> 00:12:24.701
Just tiny little
splish-splash-splish.

00:12:24.701 --> 00:12:26.033
And he walked over to my desk

00:12:26.033 --> 00:12:28.767
and you heard the little splish
and the splash.

00:12:28.767 --> 00:12:30.234
And he said to me,
he said, "Sir,

00:12:30.234 --> 00:12:31.934
I'm crying because I'm begging
for your endorsement

00:12:31.934 --> 00:12:33.834
and also because I have
a tiny little...

00:12:33.834 --> 00:12:34.901
-Pecker.

00:12:34.901 --> 00:12:36.801
[ Laughter ]
-[Normal voice] This...

00:12:36.801 --> 00:12:38.334
has been "A Closer Look."

00:12:38.334 --> 00:12:40.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:41.467
♪♪

